 "XML": [
  "Extensible Markup Language Appendix S: Concept of OperationsAnnotated Outline The number of scenarios, use cases,",
  "DRMs discussed should cover both nominal and off-nominal conditions and cover all expected functions and capabilities. A good practice is to label each of these scenarios to facilitate requirements traceability; e.g., [DRM-0100], [DRM- 0200], etc. 6.1 Nominal Conditions These scenarios, use cases,",
  "DRMs cover how the envi sioned system will operate under normal circumstances where there are no problems",
  "anomalies taking place. 6.2 Off-Nominal Conditions These scenarios cover cases where some condition has occurred that will need the system to perform in a way that is different from normal. This would cover failures, low performance, unexpected environmental conditions,",
  "operator errors. These scenarios should reveal any additional capabilities",
  "safeguards that are needed in the system. 7.0 Impact Considerations This section describes the potential impacts, both positive and negative, on the environment and other areas. 7.1 Environmental Impacts Describes how the envisioned system could impact the environment of the local area, state, country, world wide, space, and other planetary bodies as appropriate for the systems intended purpose. This includes the pos sibility of the generation of any orbital debris, potential contamination of other planetary bodies",
  "atmosphere, and generation of hazardous wastes that will need dis posal on earth and other factors. Impacts should cover the entire life cycle of the system from development through disposal. 7.2 Organizational Impacts Describes how the envisioned system could impact existing",
  "future organizational aspects. This would include the need for hiring specialists",
  "operators, specialized",
  "widespread training",
  "retraining, and use of multiple organizations. 7.3 Scientific/Technical Impacts This subsection describes the anticipated scientific",
  "technical impact of a successful mission",
  "deploy ment, what scientific questions will be answered, what knowledge gaps will be filled, and what services will be provided. If the purpose of this system is to improve oper ations",
  "logistics instead of science, describe the antici pated impact of the system in those terms. 8.0 Risks and Potential Issues This section describes any risks and potential issues asso ciated with the development, operations",
  "disposal of the envisioned system. Also includes concerns/risks with the project schedule, staffing support,",
  "implementation approach. Allocate subsections as needed for each risk",
  "issue consideration. Pay special attention to closeout issues at the end of the project. This part lists each acronym used in the ConOps and spells it out. Appendix B: Glossary of Terms The part lists key terms used in the ConOps and provides a description of their meaning."
 ]
